00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Ain't Them Bodies Saints is a 2013 American romantic crime
drama film written and directed by David Lowery.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
The film stars Casey Affleck as Bob Muldoon, Rooney Mara as
Ruth Guthrie, and Ben Foster as Patrick Wheeler.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
Bob (Affleck) and Ruth (Mara) are a couple who become involved in criminal
activities and are caught, with Bob taking the blame and going to prison.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
The film follows the events after the criminal activities as Ruth gives
birth to their daughter, and the two live comfortably.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
When the child is nearly four, Bob escapes from jail and
goes looking to reconnect with his family.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The film debuted at the 2013 Sundance Film Festival, where
it won the Cinematography Award in the U.S.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Dramatic Category and got nominated for the Grand Jury Prize.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It was selected to compete in the Critics' Week
section at the 2013 Cannes Film Festival.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
It was released on August 16, 2013, by IFC Films.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film received positive reviews overall, with critics praising its original take on the Bonnie
and Clyde archetype, and commending its style and western iconography influences.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
It garnered numerous critical awards and nominations and was listed in the top ten films of 2013 by many
domestic and international film publications, but ultimately under-performed at the box office.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of river, 1970s, texas,
family relationships, prison escape.

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
The tone is emotional.
